problems.q:
Inputs a, b, c; g1 = AND(a, c); g2 = OR(a, b); g3 = OR(g1, g2); g4 = NOR(g2, g3); g5 = NOR(a, g4); primary output g5. Targeting a stuck-at-0, the D-algorithm has reached the assignment a = 1, b = 1, c = X and implied every value it can. What is the D-frontier?

A) {g1, g2}

B) {g1, g5}

C) {g2}

D) {g1}

Inputs a, b, c, d; g1 = NAND(b, d); g2 = NAND(a, c); g3 = AND(g1, g2); g4 = AND(b, g3); primary output g4. Targeting d stuck-at-0, the D-algorithm has reached the assignment a = X, b = 1, c = 1, d = 1 and implied every value it can. What is the D-frontier?

A) {g2, g3}

B) {g3}

C) {g1, g3}

D) {g1}

Inputs a, b, c; g1 = OR(a, b); g2 = AND(c, g1); g3 = NOR(b, c); g4 = NOR(g2, g3); g5 = NAND(g2, g4); primary output g5. Targeting g1 stuck-at-0, the D-algorithm has reached the assignment a = 1, b = X, c = X and implied every value it can. What is the D-frontier?

A) {g3}

B) {g2, g4}

C) {g2, g3}

D) {g2}

Inputs a, b, c; g1 = NOR(a, c); g2 = NAND(a, g1); g3 = OR(b, g2); g4 = OR(a, g3); g5 = OR(g2, g4); primary output g5. The D-algorithm has assigned c = 0, g1 = 1, g4 = 1; every other line is X, and values have been implied forward from the assigned lines. Which gates form the J-frontier?

A) {g1, g4}

B) {g2}

C) {g1, g2, g4}

D) {g1, g3, g4}

Inputs a, b, c; g1 = NAND(a, c); g2 = AND(b, g1); g3 = AND(a, g2); g4 = NAND(g1, g3); primary output g4. The D-algorithm has assigned a = 0, g2 = 0, g4 = 1; every other line is X, and values have been implied forward from the assigned lines. Which gates form the J-frontier?

A) {g3}

B) {g2}

C) {g2, g4}

D) {g4}

Inputs a, b, c, d; g1 = AND(c, d); g2 = OR(b, d); g3 = AND(a, g2); g4 = NOR(g1, g3); g5 = AND(g2, g4); g6 = OR(g3, g5); primary output g6. The D-algorithm has assigned g1 = 0, g2 = 1; every other line is X, and values have been implied forward from the assigned lines. Which gates form the J-frontier?

A) {g3}

B) {g1, g2, g3}

C) {g1, g2}

D) {g1, g2, g4}
